    "result_text": "The entire test suite is green: **272 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp08Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the requirement that a newly created owner defaults its `registrationDate` to today's date, returned in ISO format (`YYYY-MM-DD`).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, plus getter/setter.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, set the registration date to `LocalDate.now()` when the incoming owner has none. Guarding on null preserves any date already present rather than overwriting it.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` response schema. The OpenAPI generator produces the DTO field as a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`, and MapStruct auto-maps it from the entity.\n\n4. **`resources/db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table across all four database dialects.\n\nThe date-defaulting behavior lives in the create path only (the field is read-only in the API and absent from `OwnerFields`), so updates and reads pass it straight through. The `format: date` mapping guarantees the ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` serialization the spec asks for.",
